(a) such Executable Form must also be made available as Source Code Form, as described in Section 3.1, and You must inform recipients of the Executable Form how they can obtain a copy of such Source Code Form by reasonable means in a medium customary in the software exchange; and

(b) You may give notice in the Executable Form that offers the Source Code Form in return for a fee or other compensation.

3.3. Distribution of a Larger Work

If You distribute a Larger Work, then the requirements of this License that apply to the Covered Software in that Larger Work also apply to the Larger Work as a whole. These requirements apply to the Larger Work as a whole in the same way they apply to the Covered Software, with the proviso that the notice described in Section 3.4(b) must be replaced with a notice that describes what rights are granted by this License, and must describe any notice or instructions that You provide to recipients regarding third-party works that are included in or with the Larger Work. If the Larger Work consists solely of Covered Software, this License will apply to the entire Larger Work. If the Larger Work includes combinations of Covered Software and other software, this License will apply only to those portions of the Larger Work that are Covered Software.

3.4. Redistribution Contributions

If You create or distribute a Derivative Work or Combined Work, You must make it clear that any Contribution by a Contributor in such Covered Software is not a Contribution by You.

3.5. Notice of License

You must include a copy of this License with every copy of the Covered Software You distribute, including where the Covered Software is distributed as part of a product that is made, sold, or leased as a single product. This License must be included in a manner that allows recipients to use, modify and redistribute the Source Code Form as permitted by the terms of this License. You may include a copy of this License in any form (including by way of a hyperlink) that is customary in the software industry.

3.6. Use of Contributor Name

You must not use the names, trademarks, service marks, or logos of any Contributor to endorse or promote products derived from the Covered Software except as required for reasonable and customary use in describing the origin of the work and reproducing the content of the NOTICE file.

3.7. No Additional Restrictions

